Subject: [PATCH] ntpd: do not dereference a NULL interface after a bind failure

update_interfaces() creates an endpoint for every new local address. When
create_interface() cannot open a socket for one, it returns NULL, and the
error path then logged stoa(&ep->sin) with that NULL pointer. ntpd dies
with SIGSEGV whenever a local address cannot be bound, for example an IPv6
address that is still tentative during duplicate address detection: at
start, or on the rescan after a network interface comes up.

Name the address of the endpoint that failed, ep2, in both the debug print
and the log message.

Upstream: present in ntp-4.2.8p18; upstream status not checked.
---
 ntpd/ntp_io.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/ntpd/ntp_io.c
+++ b/ntpd/ntp_io.c
@@ -1921,11 +1921,11 @@
 		}
 		else {
 			DPRINT_INTERFACE(3,
-				(ep, "updating ", " new - FAILED"));
+				(ep2, "updating ", " new - FAILED"));
 
 			msyslog(LOG_ERR,
 				"cannot bind address %s",
-				stoa(&ep->sin));
+				stoa(&ep2->sin));
 		}
 		free(ep2);
 	}
